\"/></g><g id=\"patch_8\"><path d=\"M 45.676438 138.336 L 391.636437 138.336 \" style=\"fill: none; stroke: #cccccc; stroke-width: 0.8; stroke-linejoin: miter; stroke-linecap: square\"/></g><g id=\"text_13\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(87.332487 27.490759) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" d=\"M 493 4083 Q 448 4128 493 4179 Q 691 4397 924 4537 Q 1158 4678 1420 4745 Q 1683 4813 1971 4813 Q 2470 4813 2825 4656 Q 3181 4499 3376 4227 Q 3571 3955 3571 3610 Q 3571 3264 3356 2985 Q 3142 2707 2758 2573 Q 2688 2547 2688 2528 Q 2688 2509 2758 2483 Q 3021 2413 3241 2249 Q 3462 2086 3590 1849 Q 3718 1613 3718 1312 Q 3718 915 3513 601 Q 3309 288 2902 112 Q 2496 -64 1888 -64 Q 1568 -64 1280 9 Q 992 83 745 236 Q 499 390 288 614 Q 262 646 268 672 Q 275 698 307 723 L 582 941 Q 627 973 646 966 Q 666 960 685 941 Q 877 742 1069 627 Q 1261 512 1472 457 Q 1683 403 1933 403 Q 2496 403 2803 652 Q 3110 902 3110 1293 Q 3110 1600 2937 1811 Q 2765 2022 2489 2131 Q 2214 2240 1907 2240 L 1338 2246 Q 1261 2246 1261 2310 L 1261 2643 Q 1261 2701 1338 2707 L 1798 2714 Q 2131 2714 2396 2829 Q 2662 2944 2816 3139 Q 2970 3334 2970 3584 Q 2970 3802 2842 3974 Q 2714 4147 2490 4249 Q 2266 4352 1978 4352 Q 1645 4352 1363 4224 Q 1082 4096 832 3859 Q 806 3827 780 3827 Q 755 3827 717 3859 L 493 4083 L 493 4083 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-83\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-80\" transform=\"translate(110.59375 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_14\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(170.881787 37.540966) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" d=\"M 2131 4813 Q 2598 4813 2950 4649 Q 3302 4486 3500 4192 Q 3699 3898 3699 3507 Q 3699 3206 3545 2969 Q 3392 2733 3053 2496 Q 2957 2432 3046 2394 Q 3341 2278 3529 2112 Q 3718 1946 3814 1731 Q 3910 1517 3910 1261 Q 3910 858 3683 557 Q 3456 256 3053 96 Q 2650 -64 2112 -64 Q 1587 -64 1196 83 Q 806 230 598 508 Q 390 787 390 1178 Q 390 1517 560 1789 Q 730 2061 1120 2304 Q 1197 2349 1200 2377 Q 1203 2406 1126 2445 Q 947 2547 809 2688 Q 672 2829 595 3014 Q 518 3200 518 3437 Q 518 3827 720 4137 Q 922 4448 1286 4630 Q 1651 4813 2131 4813 L 2131 4813 z\nM 2138 4365 Q 1850 4365 1613 4249 Q 1376 4134 1238 3939 Q 1101 3744 1101 3488 Q 1101 2906 1760 2758 L 2419 2605 Q 2509 2579 2633 2649 Q 2758 2720 2880 2854 Q 3002 2989 3078 3161 Q 3155 3334 3155 3514 Q 3155 3891 2880 4128 Q 2605 4365 2138 4365 L 2138 4365 z\nM 2144 384 Q 2675 384 2988 614 Q 3302 845 3302 1235 Q 3302 1530 3142 1715 Q 2982 1901 2624 1984 L 1792 2189 Q 1696 2214 1555 2153 Q 1414 2093 1273 1961 Q 1133 1830 1033 1648 Q 934 1466 934 1248 Q 934 838 1244 611 Q 1555 384 2144 384 L 2144 384 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-88\" transform=\"translate(93 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(253.186713 32.515862) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" d=\"M 2470 4678 Q 2502 4717 2534 4733 Q 2566 4749 2630 4749 L 3059 4749 Q 3136 4749 3136 4672 L 3136 1792 Q 3136 1734 3187 1734 L 3789 1734 Q 3878 1734 3878 1670 L 3878 1357 Q 3878 1274 3789 1274 L 3194 1274 Q 3136 1274 3136 1210 L 3136 96 Q 3136 0 3034 0 L 2598 0 Q 2515 0 2515 83 L 2515 1229 Q 2515 1274 2458 1274 L 384 1274 Q 288 1274 288 1357 L 288 1683 Q 288 1728 313 1776 Q 339 1824 390 1894 L 2470 4678 L 2470 4678 z\nM 2445 1734 Q 2502 1734 2502 1779 L 2502 3910 Q 2502 3987 2483 3993 Q 2464 4000 2413 3936 L 851 1818 Q 787 1734 896 1734 L 2445 1734 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-82\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(106.40625 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #333333\" transform=\"translate(335.732263 14.928) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-81\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-84\" transform=\"translate(46.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#LibreFranklin-Regular-85\" transform=\"translate(111.40625 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pc7fec62301\"><rect x=\"45.676437\" y=\"10.824\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"127.512\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Trays per hour by step","note":null},"answer":"<p>Cooking is the bottleneck at 118 trays an hour: 377.6k trays, <b>362.5k good</b>, against demand of 440k.</p> <p>Packing is already the fastest step (145/hour). Making it faster changes nothing: output stays at 362.5k. <b>Zero extra meals.</b></p> <p><b>So-what:</b> the robot can only be justified on labour savings, not on growth.</p>"},{"q":"Alternatives: an extra kettle to make cooking 18% faster ($180k), and a second blast-freezer to add 15% freezing capacity ($220k). Evaluate.","exhibit":{"kind":"table","headers":["Option","Cost ($k)","Bottleneck after","Good trays (k)","Extra contribution ($k/yr)"],"rows":[["Packing robot","600","Cook","362.5","0"],["Faster cooking","180","Blast freeze","380.9","74"],["Faster cooking + second freezer","400","Prep","399.4","147"]],"title":"Exhibit 2 · Options compared","note":null,"align":["l","r","r","r","r"],"boldLast":false},"answer":"<p><b>Cooking only:</b> 139/hour, but the blast freezer (124/hour) becomes the bottleneck: 380.9k good trays, +18.4k, $74k a year, payback 2.4 years.</p> <p><b>Cooking and freezer:</b> both are now above 130/hour, so <b>prep becomes the bottleneck</b>: 399.4k good trays, +36.9k, $147k a year for $400k: payback <b>2.7 years</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> this line is nearly balanced, so each fix only moves the limit to the next step. Even with both, Glacier is 40.6k trays short. Prep is manual, so the cheap next step is an extra prep worker per shift (to 150/hour). Cooking is then the limit again at about 427.7k good trays; the last 12.3k need around 90 hours of weekend overtime a year.</p>"},{"q":"The operations director says the robot also saves four packers' wages. How do you handle that?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Fair point: it's a cost-saving project, not a growth project, and should be judged on its own payback (four packers' wages vs $600k). It may still be worth doing later. But growth depends on cooking, freezing and prep, so those come first.</p>"}],"reco":"Don't buy the packing robot to grow: packing isn't the bottleneck, so it adds no meals. Instead add a kettle and a second blast-freezer: output rises from 362.5k to 399.4k good trays, adding about $147k a year and paying back in 2.7 years. Prep then becomes the limit: an extra prep worker per shift takes output to about 427.7k, and weekend overtime covers the rest. Evaluate the robot separately as a labour-saving project. Risk: freezer temperature compliance can't be compromised for speed. Next step: confirm the freezer supplier's lead time.","great":["Rejects the proposal with numbers, not opinion","Sees the line is nearly balanced: each fix moves the bottleneck to the next step","Separates growth projects from cost projects","Handles the director's objection respectfully"],"id":49,"slug":"glacier-meals"}